From 1950bf40f9a333bd4e3a31ee8389e1c40cf0bdcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:45:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] fix: verify a checkout's whole Lean manifest before an
 explicit view runs

Mounting the recorded overrides left one gap: a checkout whose index was stale,
or a shared package present at another revision, would start and resolve
whatever the shared directory happened to hold. `--lean-view` now reads the
checkout's manifest, resolves every pinned package to the path it will actually
see -- its override, or the declared packages directory -- re-rooting the
image's absolute links, and refuses to launch when a package is missing or sits
at another revision. The message names the pin, what was found and the
provisioner to re-run.

Both DSL checkouts are now launched explicitly in the documentation, including
`lean-cas-dsl`, whose revision the shared directory happens to hold: the shared
copy of `lean_categories` is the published image's own, provisioning neither
links nor deletes it, and neither checkout is expected to resolve through it.

Verified concurrently with the two explicit invocations: lean-cas-dsl resolved
lean_categories eea5c7f3... and lean-cas-dsl-leaf-contracts 82d1370d..., each its
own pin, both importing Mathlib ("Nat.add_comm : forall (n m : Nat), n + m =
m + n"), exit 0. Pointing lean-cas-dsl's index entry at the other revision makes
the launch stop with "pins lean_categories at eea5c7f3... but resolves
82d1370d... from .../lean_categories@82d1370d..." instead of running.
